<title>NORWAY: Fokus Q1 results rise.</title>
<headline>Fokus Q1 results rise.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three months to March 31</p>
<p>			    (millions of crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Net interest, credit commissions   236.7    vs     227.9</p>
<p> Total other operating income	 147.5    vs	97.0</p>
<p> Total other operating expenses     212.2    vs     201.2</p>
<p>Operating result before losses/</p>
<p> writedowns				 172.0    vs     123.7</p>
<p> Net loan losses			   10.3		 7.0</p>
<p>Result from ordinary operations</p>
<p> after tax				  182.5    vs     116.6</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of Norway's fourth largest bank is Fokus Bank ASA. The bank moved forward the date for its first-quarter result announcement from April 25 because 16 savings banks made a hostile takeover bid for it on Monday.</p>
<p>--Rolf Soderlind, Oslo newsroom +47 22 42 50 41</p>
</text>
